======================================================================
PART 1: The 7&21 catalog -- arithmetic checks
======================================================================
dim E7        = 133      7*19 = 133   -> 7 | dim?  True
rank E7       = 7
roots         = 126    = 18*7 = 126  -> 7|126?   True
pos roots     = 63     = 9*7 = 63   -> 7|63?    True
exponents     = [1, 5, 7, 9, 11, 13, 17]  -> is 7 an exponent? True
  middle exponent (h/2 symmetry): exponents sum to 63 ; pairs m+m'=h=18? [(1, 17), (5, 13), (7, 11), (9, 9), (11, 7), (13, 5), (17, 1)]
degrees       = [2, 6, 8, 10, 12, 14, 18]  -> degree 8 = 7+1 present? True
Coxeter h     = 18    (NOT divisible by 7: False)
|Weyl(E7)|    = 2903040 ; divisible by 7? True; by 7^2? False
  |Weyl(E7)| factorization = {2: 10, 3: 4, 5: 1, 7: 1}  (expected 2^10*3^4*5*7)
minuscule rep = 56 = 2*28 = 56 ; = 7*8 = 56  -> BOTH hold: 56 = 2*28 (antipodal pairs) AND 56 = 7*8 (Fano lines x tripartite)

--- Where does 21 genuinely appear? ---
C(7,2) = 21 = dim so(7) (antisymmetric 7x7).  21 | ?
  Under G2: 21 = 14 + 7  ->  True  (dim G2=14, vector 7). SOURCED (Baez).
C(7,3) = 35 = 35 = dim of 3-forms on R^7 (the G2 associative 3-form lives here).
The binomial tower on the Fano 7-set: C(7,1),C(7,2),C(7,3) = 7,21,35 = 7,21,35.
  7+21+35 = 63 ; note 56-rep weight under SL(2)^7? 56 = ?   (56 != 7+21+35=63; the 7+21+35 is the EXTERIOR algebra of F_2^7 truncated, NOT the 56). So 21 in E7 = dim so(7), a SUBALGEBRA fact, distinct from the 56.

--- 21 in tournaments / strong-component side ---
non-strong 6-vertex tournament classes = 21 (sourced, A051337-ish).  strong = 35, total = 56.  35+21 = 56.
  So on the TOURNAMENT side: 56 (T(6)) = 35 strong + 21 non-strong = C(7,3)+C(7,2).
  This MIRRORS the E7 binomial tower numerically. Flagged for verdict.

======================================================================
PART 2: OCF forbidden 7 -- the Phi_3(2) / Fano / K3 facts (arithmetic)
======================================================================
Phi_3(2) = 2^2+2+1 = 7  = 2^3-1 = 7 = M_3 (Mersenne) = |PG(2,2)| Fano points
I(K3, z) = 1 + 3z  (K3 = triangle conflict graph, 3 vertices pairwise adjacent => alpha_0=1, alpha_1=3, alpha_2=0)
I(K3, 2) = 1 + 3*2 = 7  = the forbidden H value 7.  So 7 = I(K3,2) = Phi_3(2). CHECK.
21 = 3 * 7 = 21 = 3 * Phi_3(2).  Forbidden because only factorization routes through 7.
Note: the '3' in K3 = A2 root system / smallest cyclotomic Phi_3 / the 3-cycle. Phi_3(2)=7 ties the SMALLEST cyclotomic to the SMALLEST projective plane.

======================================================================
PART 3: The 'exceptional cluster gas' -- is the E7 quartic a partition sum gated by 7?
======================================================================
OCF partition function:  Z = I(Omega,2) = sum_k alpha_k * 2^k   (hard-core lattice gas).
  - lives at FUGACITY 2; degree in z = independence/clique number of conflict graph Omega.
  - cluster expansion (Mayer): log Z = sum over connected subgraphs (Witt/necklace W_k).

E7 quartic Cartan invariant I4 (Duff-Ferrara 2007, PRD 76 025018):
  - DEGREE 4 in the 56 charges; SL(2)^7-covariant.
  - 56 = 7 lines x 8 (each line = a tripartite 2x2x2 system).
  - I4 = (combination of) the 7 Cayley hyperdeterminants Det(line_i), one per Fano line.
  - each Cayley hyperdeterminant of a 2x2x2 tensor is itself DEGREE 4 (Cayley's = 3-tangle).

STRUCTURAL COMPARISON TABLE
feature                          | OCF gas Z=I(Omega,2)           | E7 quartic I4                 
----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
index set                        | cliques/indep sets of Omega    | 7 lines of Fano PG(2,2)       
local object                     | a k-clique (z^k term)          | a 2x2x2 tripartite tensor     
local invariant                  | monomial 2^k                   | Cayley hyperdet (deg 4)       
global = sum of                  | alpha_k 2^k over k             | Det over 7 Fano lines         
gating prime                     | 7=Phi3(2)=I(K3,2) FORBIDDEN    | 7 = #lines = rank = #qubits   
degree                           | = clique number (varies)       | fixed 4 (quartic)             
role of 7                        | forbidden VALUE of Z           | STRUCTURAL count of summands  

CRITICAL DISTINCTION:
 - In OCF, 7 is a FORBIDDEN OUTPUT VALUE of the partition function (Z never equals 7).
 - In E7, 7 is the NUMBER OF TERMS/SUMMANDS (Fano lines) building the invariant.
 - These are DIFFERENT ROLES for 7. Same numeral, different semantic slot.
 - BUT both 7's descend from the SAME object: PG(2,2). OCF's 7 = I(K3,2)=|PG(2,2)| as a
   VALUE; E7's 7 = the 7 lines of PG(2,2) as an INDEX SET. The Fano plane is the common root.

======================================================================
PART 4: LRC(14) = 2*7 -- where is the 7?
======================================================================
LRC(14): modulus 14 = 2*7. s(t)=sin(pi t/7)/(pi t) vanishes IFF 7|t (the 7-vanishing).
period of sign(s) = 14 = 2*7. 7 = the half-period (the 'forbidden' residue class).
So LRC's 7 = the modulus's odd part = where the singular-series kernel VANISHES.
This is a THIRD distinct role: 7 as a MODULUS / vanishing locus, not a value, not a count.

THREE ROLES OF 7, made explicit:
  OCF:  7 = a forbidden VALUE of H  (7 = I(K3,2) = Phi_3(2))
  E7:   7 = the COUNT of Fano lines / rank / qubits (structural index)
  LRC:  7 = the odd MODULUS / vanishing locus (s(t)=0 iff 7|t)
Common ancestor candidate: 7 = 2^3-1 = Phi_3(2) = |PG(2,2)|. The Fano plane is the only
object that appears LITERALLY in two of three (OCF value via I(K3,2)=|PG(2,2)|; E7 via
octonion/qubit Fano lines). LRC's 7 is just the odd part of 14 -- no Fano structure shown.
